    <string name="privacy_subtitle">Before continuing, please read and accept how Keeply handles your information.</string>
    <string name="privacy_accept">I accept the privacy notice</string>
    <string name="privacy_decline">Decline and exit</string>
    <string name="privacy_close">Close</string>
    <string name="privacy_accepted_on">You accepted on %1$s</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Last updated: September 2026\n\n1. Who we are\nKeeply is a personal inventory app for tracking household products (medicines, cleaning, kitchen, and more) on your device.\n\n2. Data we process\nKeeply may store locally:\n• Optional profile (name, age, blood type, phone, email, and notes).\n• Inventory (name, category, brand, form, unit, quantities, expiration, barcode, location, notes, and photos).\n• App preferences (notifications, filters, and custom options).\n• Record of acceptance of this notice (date and version).\n\n3. Purpose\nWe use that data only to:\n• Display and manage your inventory.\n• Send local alerts you configure (expiration, stock, etc.).\n• Improve capture (photo, OCR, and barcodes on device).\n\n4. Storage and transfers\nYour profile and inventory data are stored locally. Keeply does not create an account or back up that data to the cloud in this version. ML Kit processes images, text and codes on device; Google does not receive the content or results. ML Kit SDKs may send encrypted device and app information, per-installation identifiers and technical usage metrics to Google for diagnostics, security and service improvements. We do not sell or share your personal data for advertising.\n\n5. System permissions\n• Camera: to photograph products and scan codes.\n• Photos: the system picker only grants access to the image you choose, not to your whole gallery.\n• Notifications: only if you enable them in Settings.\nYou can revoke these permissions in Android settings; some features will become unavailable.\n\n6. Retention and deletion\nData remains while you use the app or until you delete it (for example by removing products or uninstalling Keeply).\n\n7. Minors\nKeeply is intended for a general audience and is not specifically directed at children under 13. If a minor uses it, they should be supervised by a responsible adult.\n\n8. Changes to this notice\nIf we update this notice in a material way, we will ask you to accept it again before continuing.\n\n9. Contact\nFor privacy questions related to Keeply, use the contact email published on the Google Play listing.\n\nBy tapping “I accept”, you confirm that you have read and accept this notice.</string>

